## When to Use
- After using ShapeLibraryTool to identify shapes you want to use
- When you need defaultProperties, defaultSize, or customPropertyDescriptors for AddBlock

## Input
Array of \`Shapes\` entries. Each entry pairs a \`ToolboxId\` (from ShapeLibraryTool) with the \`Library\` it came from. Pairing per-entry lets you batch shapes from different libraries (e.g. flowchart.js and uml.js) in a single call. The library context is what enables variant resolution — without it, only the bare class is looked up and variant-specific defaults (size, lane count, orientation) are not applied.

